/tmp/tmp.pQ0SaJ6gqm/src/envelopeV2.tex:489:	This isomorphism is given by the following recipe: Given a map $s=(s_X,s_Y)$, we write uniquely $s_X(g)=d_X(g)p_X(g)$ and $s_Y(g)=d_Y(g)p_Y(g)$ for diagonals $d_X,d_Y$ and permutations $p_X,p_Y$. Then it is easy to check that the function $g\mapsto (d_X(g),d_Y(g))$ is a 1-cocycle with values in $D_X\times D_Y$. See Appendix \ref{appA} and Theorem \ref{class_sect} for more details.\\
