/tmp/tmp.pQ0SaJ6gqm/src/envelopeV2.tex:795:   \section{Example of $H^1$-development - Paley's Conference and Hadamard matrices.} \label{sec:paley}
/tmp/tmp.pQ0SaJ6gqm/src/envelopeV2.tex:796:   The Paley Hadamard and conference matrices were introduced in the 1933 paper \cite{Paley33}. The construction there uses Legendre symbols over prime powers. To date this is the most dense known family of Hadamard matrices. Here we will reconstruct and reinterpret these matrices using our cohomology machinary.  
