/tmp/tmp.pQ0SaJ6gqm/src/envelopeV2.tex:1387:	Recall that we construct Cohomology-Developed matrices (CDM) by computing monomial covers 
/tmp/tmp.pQ0SaJ6gqm/src/envelopeV2.tex:1417:    There are two equivalent methods to construct $H^2$-developed matrices.
/tmp/tmp.pQ0SaJ6gqm/src/envelopeV2.tex:1419:    	\item[Method I:] Compute extensions \eqref{ext7} and then replace $G$ with a cover $\widetilde{G}$ acting permutationally on $X$ and $Y$. The construction will proceed by $H^1$-development with respect to $\widetilde{G}$, using machinery of \S 3 to compute CDMs. But beware that not all extensions $\widetilde{G}$ will work. In any suitable extension, $Z$ must be mapped to $Triv$ by the constructed monomial cover. We will see below that this is a significant constraint.\\
