/tmp/tmp.pQ0SaJ6gqm/src/envelopeV2.tex:1730:    To this end, we may construct a monomial cover by Method I with $G=\widetilde{G}$, to get a $(P,P)$-action. More concretely:
/tmp/tmp.pQ0SaJ6gqm/src/envelopeV2.tex:1766:			\item[(i)]  We can construct matrices $A\in M\mu_n(N)$ invariant under the action of $\widehat{G}$.
/tmp/tmp.pQ0SaJ6gqm/src/envelopeV2.tex:1786:	By a $G$-set we mean a set $X$ with a given action of a group $G$. Given a $\{0,1\}$-matrix $|A|$ of size $N\times N$ with a group homomorphism $G\to PermAut(|A|)$, we may view its rows or columns as $G$-sets. Converesely, given two $G$-sets $X$ and $Y$ of cardinality $N$, we form the product $X\times Y$ construct a matrix $|A|$ as in Lemma \ref{25} (i.e. with $\mu_n=\mu_1$) with a representation $G\to PermAut(|A|)$. This motivates the following definition.\\
/tmp/tmp.pQ0SaJ6gqm/src/envelopeV2.tex:1830:	When $A$ is nonsingular and irreducible, this is precisely the case where sequence \eqref{ext} splits, and there is a section $s:G\to G'\subset \widetilde{G}$. The way we will solve Problem \ref{prob1} is to first find all apropriate groups $G'$, and then use the orbit construction in Lemma \ref{25} to find all $A$.\\
/tmp/tmp.pQ0SaJ6gqm/src/envelopeV2.tex:1845:	The algorithm produces all matrices $A$, together with a group $G'\subset \Aut(A)$ mapping isomprphically to $G\subseteq \PermAut(|A|)$, up to diagonal equivalence. More precisely, for every cohomology class $[z]$ of a cocyle $z$ generated by line 8 of the algorithm, a subset $\mathcal A_z \subset \mathcal A(X,Y)$ is generated. $\mathcal A_z$ depends on the choice of $z$ in the following sense: It $z'$ is cohomologous to $z$, there exist two diagonal matrices $D_L,D_R\in \mu_n^N$ such that $\mathcal A_{z'}=D_L\mathcal A_z D_R$.
/tmp/tmp.pQ0SaJ6gqm/src/envelopeV2.tex:1848:		The complexity of the algorithm is $$O(N^nn^2\# G\#Hom(H_X,\mu_n)\#Hom(H_Y,\mu_n)).$$
